    "caveats": [
      "Verify the exact physiological shear target against primary literature for first-order human retinal arterioles (reported range ~1-5 Pa); 2 Pa is a mid-range assumption.",
      "Confirm medium viscosity (assumed 1e-3 Pa·s); serum-containing medium is slightly higher (~0.9-1.1e-3), which would shift shear by the same factor.",
      "HUVEC is a generic endothelial line; for retinal fidelity use primary human retinal microvascular endothelial cells (HRMEC) or a retinal-specific line, and re-validate the shear-response phenotype.",
      "The 100×100 µm square channel is an approximation of a ~100-150 µm round arteriole; a round or semi-circular cross-section would better match the true lumen geometry and shear distribution.",
      "Confirm the syringe pump can deliver 20 µL/min stably and that the 800 Pa (~6 mmHg) pressure drop is within the device/tubing sealing limits.",
      "High shear (2 Pa) is a stress condition for HUVEC (registry range 0.1-1 Pa); include a low-shear (e.g. 0.1-0.5 Pa) control to isolate shear-specific responses."
    ]
  },
